---
description: No in-memory collections or untranslatable methods in IQueryable
alwaysApply: true
---

# LINQ-to-EF

When working with `IQueryable` and Entity Framework Core:

- **Never** filter by in-memory collections (e.g. `myHashSet.Contains(x)`) inside an `IQueryable` pipeline
- **Never** call C# methods that EF cannot translate (e.g. custom normalizers) inside an `IQueryable` pipeline
- EF Core cannot translate these to SQL

**Options:**

1. Materialize first with `ToListAsync()`, then filter in memory (LINQ-to-Objects)
2. Express the filter using only database-translatable operations (joins, SQL functions, constants)
